# Staging link

After the first push of a branch (and again if the URL slug changes), put the **stage URL in the user-facing reply**. Do not wait for the user to ask. Do not rely only on the GitHub PR comment.

## URL

- `main` → https://anrighi.github.io/sacchos-team-website/
- other branches → `https://anrighi.github.io/sacchos-team-website/preview/<slug>/`

Slug: branch name, replace every character that is not `a-zA-Z0-9._-` with `-` (so `cursor/foo-6b46` → `cursor-foo-6b46`). Trailing slash required.

CI publishes on **push** to the branch (`deploy-staging`). Wait until that job is green before treating the link as live; still include the URL as soon as the branch is pushed.

## Example

Branch `cursor/reload-expressions-6b46`:

https://anrighi.github.io/sacchos-team-website/preview/cursor-reload-expressions-6b46/
